Usage: nice [OPTION] [COMMAND [ARG]...]

Run a program with modified scheduling priority.
Run COMMAND with an adjusted niceness, which affects process scheduling.
With no COMMAND, print the current niceness. Niceness values range from
-20 (most favorable) to 19 (least favorable). Default is 10.

OPTIONS:
  -n, --adjustment ARG  adjust increment
      --help            display this help and exit
  -V, --version         output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
